[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n1_thomas"
text = "# DRAFT
# Thomas at dusk, at his herbs in the infirmary (night 1). Kind; he goes over the night's routine.
# The killing seen from the Keys (n0_saw_killing): a dream, or the kitchen's beast being bled. Never the truth.
# The guesthouse key: truthful, but he leaves locking to the porter and makes it sound unkind.
# Anselm: an old man who frightens easily. If Anselm warned him on the tour, Thomas asks what he said.
# Claims: n1_thomas_beast (lie: a man was killed by the well on night 0, not a beast; confront with window_killing).
== start
(Thomas at his bench, a mortar in his lap, grinding something that smells green. He smiles when he sees you.)
Thomas {warm}: You slept. Good. The first night is the longest; after that your body learns it.
Thomas {warm, nod}: Supper at the bell, then the gate from Cole. Bar it. Matins at the black ring, then your round, then wait for Lauds.
-> topics

== again
Thomas {warm}: Still here? The supper bell won't be long.
-> topics

== topics
* [if n0_saw_killing] [if not n1_thomas_well] Last night, from the Keys, I saw a man killed by the well. -> well
* [if not n1_thomas_key] What should I do with the guesthouse key? -> key
* [if not n1_thomas_anselm] How is Brother Anselm keeping? -> anselm

== well [set n1_thomas_well]
(He hears you out without stopping the pestle. Then he stops.)
-> well_drunk [if n0_saw_killing=drunk]
-> well_sober

== well_drunk
Thomas {warm}: You came to us this morning with Agnes's ale still in your eyes. At midnight, in rain, from the top of the Keys?
Thomas {warm, still}: They bled a beast for the kitchen by the well last night. A lantern, a knife, a thing that kicks.
Thomas {warm}: I'd have dreamed the same. But I'd not carry it to the abbot. He sleeps badly enough as it is.
* [if not read_n1_thomas_beast] It was no beast, brother. I saw a man. -> n1_thomas_beast
* (Let it go.) -> topics

== well_sober
Thomas {warm}: From the top of the Keys you look down into our court, it's true. At midnight, in the rain, after a day on a cart.
Thomas {warm, still}: The kitchen bled a beast by the well in the night, so it would hang by morning. A knife over a thing that kicks.
Thomas {warm}: I can see how it looked. I'd not carry it to the abbot, though. He sleeps badly enough as it is.
* [if not read_n1_thomas_beast] It was no beast, brother. I saw a man. -> n1_thomas_beast
* (Let it go.) -> topics

== n1_thomas_beast [claim n1_thomas_beast lie]
(He sets the pestle down, and smiles at you.)
Thomas {warm, still}: A beast, brother. I heard it from this bench, kicking and bawling. Nobody died in our court.
* [believe] Then I dreamed it. -> beast_believed
* [press] You heard it? At midnight, through the rain? -> beast_pressed
* [confront window_killing] I wrote it down that night. A man in a habit, dragging a man toward the cellar. -> beast_broken

== beast_believed
Thomas {warm, nod}: Dreams come cheap in a strange bed. Put it by, brother.
-> topics

== beast_pressed
Thomas {warm}: Through the rain, and through a shut door. A pig makes himself heard.
(He takes up the pestle again, and says no more about it.)
-> topics

== beast_broken
(For a moment his face does nothing at all. Then the smile comes back, slower.)
Thomas {grave, swallow}: You wrote it down.
Thomas {warm}: Then write beside it that it was dark, and raining, and every brother here wears a black habit. So does the man who drags a pig to the cellar to hang.
-> topics

== key [set n1_thomas_key]
Thomas {warm}: Keep it on your ring with the gate's. Show a guest to his bed, and the rest is your judgement.
Thomas {warm}: Anselm locked them in at night. Some guests took that ill, to be shut up like sheep.
Thomas {warm, nod}: Do as you think best. It's your gate now.
-> topics

== anselm [set n1_thomas_anselm]
Thomas {sad}: His eyes have gone white, both of them. I keep him here, where it's warm.
Thomas {warm, still}: He frightens easily now, and he talks. Old porters' tales. Don't let him put them in your head.
-> anselm_ask [if d1_anselm_warned]
-> topics

== anselm_ask
Thomas {warm}: Did he say something to you this morning, after I'd gone?
* He told me not to let them in after the bell. [trust thomas 5] -> anselm_told
* He only wished me well. -> anselm_kept

== anselm_told [set n1_thomas_whisper=told]
(He nods slowly, and goes back to his mortar.)
Thomas {sad}: Don't let them in after the bell. Yes. He says it to the walls, most nights. Poor soul.
-> topics

== anselm_kept [set n1_thomas_whisper=kept]
(He looks at you a moment longer than he needs to.)
Thomas {warm}: Well. He likes you, then.
-> topics

== leave
Thomas {warm}: Eat well at supper, brother. You'll be glad of it by Matins.
"
